---
title: "Architecture"
sidebar:
  order: 4
---

NAHPU is a cross-platform Flutter app with local SQLite storage and a thin Rust
bridge for operations that are better handled in shared Rust crates.

## High-level schema

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                             NAHPU App                               │
│                    Flutter UI + Dart application                    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
          │
          │ user actions, routes, forms, previews
          ▼
┌───────────────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────────────────────┐
│ lib/screens/              │     │ lib/screens/shared/              │
│ Page-level UI             │────▶│ Reusable widgets and controls    │
└───────────────────────────┘     └──────────────────────────────────┘
          │
          │ watches / reads providers
          ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ lib/services/providers/                                             │
│ Riverpod providers and AsyncNotifiers                               │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
          │
          │ calls services
          ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ lib/services/                                                       │
│ Dart business logic: database access, import/export orchestration,  │
│ media handling, file pickers, settings, platform services           │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
          │                                      │
          │ Drift queries                         │ Flutter Rust Bridge calls
          ▼                                      ▼
┌───────────────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────────────────────┐
│ lib/services/database/    │     │ lib/src/rust/                    │
│ Drift + SQLite            │     │ Generated Dart bridge bindings   │
└───────────────────────────┘     └──────────────────────────────────┘
          │                                      │
          │ local files                          │ FFI
          ▼                                      ▼
┌───────────────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────────────────────┐
│ App document directory    │     │ rust/src/api/                    │
│ SQLite DB, media, exports │     │ Thin Rust wrapper modules        │
└───────────────────────────┘     └──────────────────────────────────┘
                                                 │
                                                 │ calls crates
                                                 ▼
                              ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
                              │ NAHPU API crates                     │
                              │ nahpu_db, nahpu_export, nahpu_gis,   │
                              │ nahpu_archive, nahpu_configs         │
                              └──────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Layers

**Screens** are page-level UI wrappers. Keep them focused on rendering,
navigation, and connecting controls to providers or services.

**Shared widgets** live under `lib/screens/shared/`. Put reusable UI here when
more than one screen needs it.

**Providers** expose app state through Riverpod. NAHPU uses `AsyncNotifier`
heavily for database-backed state because it keeps loading, success, error, and
mutation behavior in one testable class.

**Services** contain business logic. Import/export, file IO, media handling,
database orchestration, and platform-specific behavior should live in
`lib/services/`, not in widgets.

**Database** code uses Drift over SQLite. The app is offline-first, so database
changes require careful schema versions, migrations, and tests.

**Rust wrappers** in `rust/src/api/` expose functionality to Dart through
Flutter Rust Bridge. Keep this layer thin.

**NAHPU API crates** contain reusable Rust implementations. The app currently
depends on crates for archive handling, database export/import, document export,
GIS output, and user configuration.

## Directory map

{% filetree %}
- android/ Android platform-specific code and build configuration
- assets/ Static assets such as images, fonts, and icons
- db_schemas/ Drift schema snapshots and migration fixtures
- integration_test/ End-to-end integration tests
- ios/ iOS platform-specific code and build configuration
- lib/ Main Dart source code for the Flutter app
  - screens/ Page-level Flutter UI
  - screens/shared/ Reusable UI components
  - services/ Business logic, providers, database, IO, export services
  - src/rust/ Generated Flutter Rust Bridge Dart bindings
- linux/ Linux platform-specific code and build configuration
- macos/ macOS platform-specific code and build configuration
- rust/ Rust wrapper crate used by Flutter Rust Bridge
  - src/api/ Thin wrapper modules exposed to Dart
- scripts/ Development and automation scripts
- test/ Unit and widget tests
- web/ Web platform-specific code and build configuration
- windows/ Windows platform-specific code and build configuration
{% /filetree %}

## Design principles

- Keep screens thin and move logic into services/providers.
- Keep Rust wrappers thin and move reusable Rust behavior into NAHPU API crates.
- Prefer local, deterministic behavior because NAHPU must work without network
  access in field conditions.
- Treat exports, imports, and migrations as data integrity features. Add tests
  when changing them.
